{
  "_about": "Every colour the 3D scene uses, after Sam_Comm_final.png: one plum ink for every outline, a warm yellow sky, salmon and coral walls, sage greens, and orbs in cool colours so they read against the warm city. Gold orbs are the ones Objection turns back. Zone two (the White Waste) adds an ice set, ice_*, after a polar dusk: pale blues and whites, navy ink, the expedition's reds and lamps, an aurora; its orbs are cobalt blue (the Injunction breaks blue orbs, and zone one's cyan) and ember, which read against the white; its enemies are navy with ember eyes. Zone three (the Glass House) adds house_* and lab_*: a mansion at night after Resident Evil's, burgundy and green wallpaper, dark wood, cream marble, brass and candlelight, moonlight in the windows, and labs of white tile, steel and green fluid; its agents wear charcoal suits and dark glasses; its orbs are scarlet, chalk white and lime, which read against the dark rooms, with cobalt and gold; the Executor is gunmetal with ember weak points, and in its last phase gold with pale eyes. Zone four (the Ascent) adds ascent_*: a mountain in the light of an evening that never ends, warm stone, moss and snow, a pink and violet dusk, cloud below; its assassins wear the player's own coat; the Pioneer mech is the expedition's red and navy; the Idiot God is violet flesh, eyes and a black maw. wards: the orb colours the Injunction breaks at each of its wards: the first with the wall itself, the second with a Standing Order, the third with a Permanent Injunction; gold is the parry's and no wall breaks it. The Ascent's creatures add fauna_*: a red deer's hide and pale bone, a rook's blue-black, a toad's olive, a carnivorous plant's greens and crimson, snowmelt blues and foam, a toadstool's orange cap, a bear's brown; corruption paints them with the Idiot God's eldritch_* and the clock's gold. Zone five (inside the Idiot God) adds god_*: violet and rose flesh, bone and teeth, dream-stone lilac, crystals of eldritch cyan, a gold for its seams, and a fog that drifts through the colours; its seven enemies keep the colours of the arts they come from: an eight-bit green (glyph_*), a vector display's cyan and pink (vector_*), an engraving's paper and ink (etching_*), a PlayStation hound's flat skin (render_*), a cartoon's black, white and red (toon_*), and a mathematician's gold (recursion_*); the Reprise is you, in negative. The trumpet is brass (trumpet_*); the lullaby's staff marks notes great, good and missed (song_*). The last mission's home adds home_*: a house on a Saturday morning, warm walls, a wood floor, rugs, a blue-grey sofa, a sage kitchen and sunlight; Chumbles is a long-haired lynx-point cat (cat_*), cream with a white ruff, grey-blue points and mask, darker ear tips, tabby lines on his forehead, blue eyes and a pink nose; hearts are pink; the yarn ball is red and the treats brown.",
